# ENG-21: agents review and approve each other's pull requests. The
# stakeholder approves the specification, the decision records, the
# scenarios and the process that builds and checks the code, listed
# below, and no Rust source. A path with no code owner here, code among
# it, merges on the approval of any reviewer other than its author,
# agent or human.

# The specification (the requirement text).
/docs/srs/                    @jeduden

# The decision records that justify design and dependencies (ENG-26).
/docs/adr/                    @jeduden

# The scenarios that make the requirement text executable.
/features/                    @jeduden

# The build configuration of every crate: its manifest, whose [lints]
# could switch the workspace bans off and whose dependencies the
# architecture check reads, and the clippy configuration that refuses
# sockets, program starts, clocks and random order in its code (SEC-01,
# ENG-16, ENG-03).
/crates/*/clippy.toml         @jeduden
/crates/*/Cargo.toml          @jeduden
/tooling/*/Cargo.toml         @jeduden

# CI, the coverage floors, the toolchain pins, the lint and supply-chain
# configuration and this file.
/.github/                     @jeduden
/scripts/                     @jeduden
/Cargo.toml                   @jeduden
/rust-toolchain.toml          @jeduden
/mise.toml                    @jeduden
/mise.lock                    @jeduden
/mise.dev.toml                @jeduden
/mise.dev.lock                @jeduden
/clippy.toml                  @jeduden
/deny.toml                    @jeduden
/codecov.yml                  @jeduden
/.mdsmith.yml                 @jeduden

# The supply-chain and disclosure policy: every new direct dependency
# needs an accepted ADR under /docs/adr/, listed in DEPENDENCIES.md
# (ENG-18), so it passes here.
/SECURITY.md                  @jeduden
/DEPENDENCIES.md              @jeduden

# The agent instructions, and the shared sections they include.
/CLAUDE.md                    @jeduden
/AGENTS.md                    @jeduden
/.claude/                     @jeduden
/docs/agents/                 @jeduden
